        "original_id": "6bd6e5a7-55e8-5a3d-ae6b-69c06b965ff8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beyazıt Tower, Miniatürk, Istanbul University Observatory, Beyazıt Square, Golden Horn, Fatih, Istanbul, Turkey\n- Organizations: Istanbul University, Ottoman Ministry of War\n- Concepts: Seraskier Tower, Forum Tauri, seven hills of Istanbul\n\nFacts:\n- Beyazıt Tower, also called Seraskier Tower, is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower in the courtyard of Istanbul University's main campus on Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Beyazıt Tower stands on one of Istanbul's seven hills, the hills on which Constantine the Great built the city following the model of Rome.\n- Beyazıt Square was known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period.\n- Istanbul University's main campus was formerly the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Istanbul University Observatory was established in 1936.\n- Istanbul University Observatory is next to the historic Beyazıt Tower within Istanbul University's main campus at Beyazıt Square in the Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Miniatürk is a miniature park on the north-eastern shore of the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
